l_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main requires code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01L76QeMeKWz4YzoFfJqvwvA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/half-even-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` is documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it was implemented with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis PR changes the rounding mode in `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It is a one-line logic change plus the matching import.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n- Expected results: `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66`, which match the test.\n\nRequesting review from @alex.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-half-even-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in a pull request against main, #101, with alex requested as reviewer. I haven't merged it.\n\n- **Root cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. The test expectations match `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/half-even-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **Pull request:** #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\nMerging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.", "type": "text"}]}]}